The rule says: 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.' For the input fence[ A B ], the fence holds A and B, so the last object inside the fence is B; recovery should be B. For the rewritten text fence[ A B ] C, the fence still holds A and B, so the last object inside the fence is still B; recovery should be B. Therefore the check's answer ought to be unchanged.
